Mix ingredients, except yeast extract, peptone, vitamins, sulfur and        Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O, and autoclave under a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20)      atmosphere.   Separately autoclave yeast extract and peptone      as 10% solutions and Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O as a 5% solution       under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere.   Steam sulfur for 3 hr on each of       3 successive days. Filter-sterilize NaHCO<sub>3</sub> as an 8%      solution and vitamin solution while gassing with N<sub>2</sub>.         Aseptically and anaerobically add yeast extract, peptone, NaHCO<sub>3</sub>      and vitamin solutions, and sulfur to the medium under a      N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20) atmosphere.      Prior to inoculation, add the sterile Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution, and       adjust pH to 6.2-6.4 with sterile 1 N H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>. <br>
